+# Trojka — Linux / modern gcc port
+
+Source: FreeBSD port `games/trojka`, distfile `trojka.tar.gz` (Maarten Los, 1989–1995).
+The untouched original is kept in `../pristine/trojka/`.
+
+## Build
+
+```sh
+make                 # gcc + ncurses
+./trojka             # play
+./trojka -s          # show high scores
+make install PREFIX=$HOME/.local
+```
+
+Needs `libncurses-dev`. Builds warning-free with
+`-std=c99 -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Wshadow -Wstrict-prototypes -Wconversion`.
+
+## What had to change
+
+The 1992 code is K&R C with almost no standard headers and relies on
+implicit declarations, all of which modern C rejects.
+
+* **ANSI prototypes everywhere.** All K&R definitions converted; the
+  cross-file declarations that used to be hand-written `int foo();` lists
+  at the top of each `.c` now live in one new header, `proto.h`.
+  Functions that never returned a value are now `void`.
+* **Missing headers added:** `stdlib.h`, `string.h`, `unistd.h`, `time.h`,
+  `sys/stat.h`.
+* **`getopt()` renamed to `parse_args()`** — it clashed with the POSIX
+  `getopt(3)` declared in `unistd.h`.
+* **Key input rewritten.** The original did `ioctl(0, FIONREAD, &count)`
+  with a `long count` and then `getchar()`. On LP64 `FIONREAD` writes an
+  `int`, so the upper half of `count` was garbage, and mixing stdio with
+  curses misbehaves on modern terminals. Now uses ncurses `nodelay()` +
+  `getch()`, which gives the same "return 0 if nothing pending" semantics.
+* **`killkeys()`** was `fflush(stdin)` (undefined behaviour on Linux,
+  and a no-op in glibc). Now `flushinp()`.
+* **`delay()`** used `usleep(ms * 1200)`, which is undefined for values
+  over 1000000 µs — `showgameover()` asks for 1500 ms, i.e. 1.8 s. Now
+  `nanosleep()`. The original 1.2 fudge factor is preserved so game speed
+  is unchanged.
+* **Score file moved** from `/usr/games/lib/trojka.scores`, which an
+  ordinary user cannot create, to `$HOME/.trojka.scores`
+  (`scorefile_path()` in `hiscore.c`). A truncated or corrupt score file
+  is now detected and reset instead of being read into the table.
+* **`selectspeed()`** fell off the end of the function without returning
+  a value when `q` was pressed. Returns 0 now.
+* **`crmode()`/`nocrmode()`** replaced with `cbreak()`/`nocbreak()`.
+* **Terminal size is checked** (80x24 minimum) for all platforms, not
+  just the old SunOS branch.
+* **Cookie messages** were written to line 25, which does not exist on a
+  standard 80x24 terminal, so they silently vanished. `mesg_row()` in
+  `screen.c` falls back to the last line.
+* **Name entry** accepts DEL (0x7f) and `KEY_BACKSPACE` as well as `^H`,
+  and the name buffer is zeroed before use.
+* **`reset_f()` is now called from `resetgame()`** — the tag shadow matrix
+  kept stale `TAGGED` entries from the previous game.
+* `statistics()` guards against a divide by zero on `blocks`.
+* Include guards fixed (`#endif _trojka_h_` is not valid C; the guard
+  macro in `trojka.h` was also misspelled, so the header had no guard).
+* `Makefile` rewritten: pkg-config for ncurses, pattern rules, a real
+  `install` target.
+
+Nothing in the game logic, scoring, layout or timing was changed.
+
+## Testing
+
+`tests/ttytest.py` drives the game inside a pseudo-terminal using `pyte` and
+prints the rendered 80x25 screen after each step, so gameplay can be
+checked without a human at the keyboard.
+
+```sh
+python3 -m venv /tmp/venv && /tmp/venv/bin/pip install pyte
+/tmp/venv/bin/python tests/ttytest.py tests/steps/steps2.txt -- ./trojka
+```
+
+Each step line is `delay<TAB>keys<TAB>label`. `TTYTEST_ROWS` /
+`TTYTEST_COLS` change the emulated terminal size; `TTYTEST_TERM`
+defaults to `vt100` because pyte does not implement the ECMA-48 `REP`
+escape that xterm's terminfo uses to compress repeated characters.
+
+To make block shapes deterministic, preload a stub `rand()`
+(see `tests/` — `fixedrand.c` always returns the same shape,
+`seqrand.c` replays a sequence from `$RANDSEQ`).
